### Justification
On October 26, 2020, the United States Senate voted 52-48 to confirm Amy Coney Barrett to the Supreme Court, as documented by [Ballotpedia](https://ballotpedia.org/Amy_Coney_Barrett_confirmation_hearings_and_votes) and reported by [CBS News](https://www.cbsnews.com/losangeles/news/scotus-amy-coney-barrett/). Following the vote, a ceremonial swearing-in was held on the South Lawn of the White House on the evening of October 26, 2020, where Senior Associate Justice Clarence Thomas administered the constitutional oath, according to [Getty Images](https://www.gettyimages.com/detail/news-photo/judge-amy-coney-barrett-talks-with-supreme-court-associate-news-photo/1282403922) and the [Supreme Court of the United States](https://www.supremecourt.gov/publicinfo/press/oath/oath_barrett.aspx). She officially became the 115th Justice of the Supreme Court, as reported by the [Associated Press](https://apnews.com/article/election-2020-donald-trump-virus-outbreak-ruth-bader-ginsburg-amy-coney-barrett-82a02a618343c98b80ca2b6bf9eafe07), and subsequently took her judicial oath the following day on October 27, 2020, to officially begin her judicial duties.